[h1]Phobos' War Has Been Declared[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.3.0
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - held draft, awaiting owner gameplay checks

Took a beating? Stand down and the ship's own build sites go back where your walls, floors, doors and machines used to be. No more re-placing a torn-up hull tile by tile. The crew still need real replacement parts and still have to do the work.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Battle stations[/b] start on their own when an enemy is engaged with your ship, your weapons lock on, or your hull takes damage, and end after 5 quiet minutes. Or call them yourself at any navigation station and keep them until you stand down.
[*]Every installed part destroyed on your ship while at battle stations is logged where it stood, vanilla and modded alike. Damaged parts are left to the game's own repair jobs.
[*]When you stand down, the game's own build sites are laid in those spots, floors first. Doors, alarms and machines come back in the state a normal install gives them.
[*]An after-action line in the crew log sums up what was laid, what was held and which loose items were lost.
[/list]

[h2]Rebuild schematics[/h2]
Unbuilt walls and machines block walking just like the real thing, so you choose what gets laid:
[list]
[*][b]Safe[/b] (default): lays only build sites the crew can walk through. Walls, doors and bulky machines are held until you choose Lay postponed build sites.
[*][b]Safe plus walls[/b]: Safe, plus walls, window walls and temporary seals, so a breached hull closes up. Doors, hatches, docking ports and bulky machines are still held.
[*][b]Everything[/b]: lays them all at once. Corridors can be cut off until the crew finish.
[*][b]Hull only[/b]: an example to copy.
[*][b]Your own[/b]: drop a schematic file in BepInEx/config/PhobosWarDeclared/schematics and match parts by ID, game condition, INSTALL tab or whether they block walking. The player guide shows the format. Schematics can also come from add-ons other players publish.
[/list]

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Right-click an intact navigation station on a ship you own for Battle stations, Stand down and Lay postponed build sites.
[*]Stock loose walls, floors and parts: build sites wait until the crew have them.
[*]In the F3 console, phoboswar status shows the log; phoboswar schematic everything switches schematic.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.104.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos' War Has Been Declared and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ordinary saves are supported. The battle log and held parts are saved with each ship.
[*]Only ships you own, and only installed parts. Loose cargo destroyed in a fight is listed, not replaced.
[*]A few unique fixtures have no install job in the game and cannot get a build site; they are listed instead.
[*]A build site that cannot be laid while you hold an item is tried again every ten real seconds; put the item away or use Lay postponed build sites.
[*]Hull damage from any cause (a collision, a burst canister) starts battle stations unless you switch that setting off.
[*]Automated checks pass; in-game checks are still pending.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games or Kitfox Games. It adds no artwork or items and uses the game's own build sites, install jobs and navigation stations.

